## 3. Checking Whether a Number Is a Four-Digit Number

A positive number is a four-digit number if it lies between 1000 and 9999.

**Condition:**

`n >= 1000 && n <= 9999`

**Program:**

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int n;

    cout << "Enter a number: ";
    cin >> n;

    if (n >= 1000 && n <= 9999) {
        cout << "Four Digit Number";
    }
    else {
        cout << "Not a Four Digit Number";
    }

    return 0;
}
```

