## 4. Checking Whether Magnitude Is Smaller Than 69

Magnitude means the absolute value of a number.

For example:
- Magnitude of -10 = 10
- Magnitude of 20 = 20

To check whether magnitude is smaller than 69:

`-69 < n && n < 69`

**Example:**

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int n;

    cout << "Enter a number: ";
    cin >> n;

    if (n > -69 && n < 69) {
        cout << "Magnitude is smaller than 69";
    }
    else {
        cout << "Magnitude is not smaller than 69";
    }

    return 0;
}
```

