## 6. Checking Whether Three Numbers Can Form a Triangle

Three positive numbers can form a triangle if the sum of any two sides is greater than the third side.

### Triangle Conditions

1. a + b > c
2. b + c > a
3. c + a > b

All three conditions must be true.

**Program:**

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int a, b, c;

    cout << "Enter three sides: ";
    cin >> a >> b >> c;

    if (a + b > c && b + c > a && c + a > b) {
        cout << "Valid Triangle";
    }
    else {
        cout << "Not a Valid Triangle";
    }

    return 0;
}
```

