## 10. Nested If-Else

Nested if-else means writing one if-else statement inside another if-else statement.

It is useful when we need to check conditions step by step.

**Syntax:**

```cpp
if (condition1) {

    if (condition2) {
        // Code
    }
    else {
        // Code
    }

}
else {
    // Code
}
```

### Example: Greatest of Three Numbers

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int a, b, c;

    cout << "Enter three numbers: ";
    cin >> a >> b >> c;

    if (a >= b) {
        if (a >= c) {
            cout << "Greatest = " << a;
        }
        else {
            cout << "Greatest = " << c;
        }
    }
    else {
        if (b >= c) {
            cout << "Greatest = " << b;
        }
        else {
            cout << "Greatest = " << c;
        }
    }

    return 0;
}
```

